  "structural_change": "S81-TILES3 10-17 (coordinator 0co: 2x2 parent with an aligned tile pitch, no gaps on link paths): wires-only parent of the four hardened KP4 decoder tiles on the 43.2-um child lattice, every seam a 21.6-um channel. Pinwheel 2x2 (cluster coords): dsyn 194.4^2 at (43.2,43.2) SW, dchn 216x194.4 at (259.2,43.2) SE (grown E from 194.4 for util, S81-TILES4), ddly 237.6x146.88 at (43.2,259.2) NW, dout 248.4x233.28 at (302.4,259.2) NE. Seams: dsyn N x_q 4.32-118.8 == ddly S w_d (same x origin, straight 21.6-um hop); dsyn E k_* == dchn W k_* (same y origin, straight); dchn N cw_q/decision -> dout S cw/decision across 21.6 um (x overlap 302.4-453.6); ddly S r_d (x 170.6-276.5) -> dout W d_q (y 263.5-384.5) through the centre channel cross (~160 um, < 405 reach). Outer white space only at the SE (right of dchn) and NW (above ddly) corners, which no link crosses. p_d W aligned to dsyn's W face, q_* E aligned to dout's E face, clk / rst_n S at the centre channel (x 246-252) between dsyn and dchn. Outline 578.88 x 518.4 (1.12:1). RTL: ot_s81_kp4_dec.sv needs the hard_define OT_KP4_DEC_HARD wrapper (children without #(.MUT)) before gen -- deferred until the dsyn/ddly e5e84db07 routes are submitted, because dec.sv is in every child's extra_paths. S81-TILES5 10-17: dsyn grows 194.4 -> 216 square (GRT-0116 corner congestion); pitch kept: dchn (280.8, 43.2), ddly (43.2, 280.8), dout (324, 280.8), 21.6-um seams unchanged; outline 600.48 x 540; p_d W 47.52-250.56 (= dsyn's W face), clk / rst_n S at the dsyn|dchn channel x 267.8-273.2, n_corr / n_unc and q_* +21.6 with dchn / dout. S81-TILES6 10-17 ~23:55: all four children CLOSED (dsyn t2-e3dea7351, dchn/ddly t2-5f0b4a343, dout t2-cef44c405; views on main); dec.sv gets the OT_KP4_DEC_HARD wrapper (children without #(.MUT)); pitch and outline unchanged (child pins checked against the view LEFs: x_q/w_d and k_* seams straight, p_d/q_*/n_* parent pins on the children's faces). LATTICE FIX: the TILES5 re-pitch put dchn/ddly at 280.8 and dout at 324 / 280.8, which are OFF the 43.2-um child lattice (gen snapped dchn onto dsyn: channel 0). With dsyn 216 (5 x 43.2) the lattice-legal pitch is dchn (302.4, 43.2) and ddly (43.2, 302.4) (43.2-um straight seams for k_* and x_q), dout (302.4, 259.2) (21.6-um seams to dchn N cw and to ddly E; dchn cw x 306.9-479.3 now left-aligned with dout cw 306.8-421.1). Outline 600.48 x 540 kept (margins E 49.7 / N 47.5). Parent pins: q_* -21.6 with dout, n_corr / n_unc +21.6 with dchn, clk / rst_n S at the dsyn|dchn channel centre (x 278.6-284.0). Risk for review: ddly r_d (S face) -> dout W d_q crosses the 43.2 dsyn|ddly seam and the 21.6-um ddly|dout channel; the trial GRT gate measures it. S81-TILES8 10-18 (coordinator 0ej: widen the 21.6-um ddly|dout channel carrying the 544-b ddly r_d -> dout W d_q link to 43.2 um; outline may grow): ddly is 237.6 = 5.5 lattice pitches wide, so with every child origin on the 43.2-um lattice the ddly E (280.8) -> dout W gap can only be 21.6 + k*43.2; dout moves x 302.4 -> 345.6 (on lattice), channel 21.6 -> 64.8 um (narrowest lattice-legal width >= 43.2; an exact 43.2 needs dout off-lattice at 324). dout y and every other child unchanged; dchn N cw (x 306.9-479.3) -> dout S cw now x 350.0-464.3, still inside dchn's span (straight 21.6-um vertical hop). Outline 600.48 -> 622.08 x 540 (+21.6; E margin 49.68 -> 28.08 >= PIN_EDGE 20 + core 2.16). Parent pins unchanged (q_* E follow dout's unchanged y; S/W pins unchanged).",
